    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d57">

                <pb facs="0118" n="36" xml:id="pg36"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>)<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d57-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1945-01-15">15 January 1945</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 168, Top Secret for Ambassador Harriman from the Secretary of State, via
                    Navy Channels.</p>
                <p>In addition to myself and Bohlen whom you know about I shall bring with me to <hi
                        rendition="#small-caps">Argonaut</hi> H. Freeman Matthews; Alger Hiss, for
                    Dumbarton Oaks matters; and four men who will act as secretaries. I will be
                    accompanied by a military aide designated by General Marshall. Bohlen asks that
                    if possible you bring Nelson Newton with you to help him in writing up the
                    minutes. If this is not possible let me know and I shall bring another male
                    stenographer.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                        <anchor n="2" xml:id="d57-f2"/>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d57-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d57-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the United States Naval Attaché, Moscow, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d57-f2" n="2" xml:id="d57-f2-content">
                <p>In reply Harriman stated that he would bring Edward Page, Jr., as an interpreter
                    and general assistant to Bohlen, and also another stenographer in place of
                    Nelson Newton, who had already left Moscow on another assignment (Roosevelt
                    Papers, telegrams from Harriman, January 16 and 18, 1945).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
